## Verification
- 298 backend tests passed; Python compilation, JavaScript syntax, and Bicep compilation passed.
- Deploy-only ARM validation passed with 0 create, 0 modify, 0 delete.
- Host indexed `process_snovio_sync` and `get_snovio_sync_status`.
- Frontend contains safe response parsing and queued sync polling.
- Exact Golda scenario reproduced safely: Copilot proposed `app_create_list`, confirmation returned list ID `40858942`, read-back verified it, and cleanup removed it.
- Natural-language list inspection now discovers and executes the correct read tool without internal tool names.
- Missing REST credentials return valid JSON 503, never an `Unexpected token` parsing error.
- Anonymous callback is 200; invalid webhook token is 401; protected API redirects to login.
- No post-deployment exceptions; all created Snov.io test data was deleted.

## Scope Note
The signed-in production test session had MCP OAuth but no saved Snov.io REST API credentials, so the full live queued REST sync was proven on the identical test-bed code and verified structurally in Cloudware. The affected Cloudware user can now save API credentials in Settings and retry safely.

